What:		/sys/devices/.../<panel>/timings
		/sys/devices/.../<panel>/timing
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	ArkOS / panel-simple maintainers
Description:

		panel-simple exposes the timings parsed from the panel's DT
		"display-timings" node through two sysfs attributes on the
		panel device. This is a vendor extension; it only exists when
		the panel node contains a "display-timings" node.

		What:		timings
		Type:		RO
		Description:	List of the available timings with their
				index, resolution, refresh rate and the
				currently active entry:

				count: 2
				0: 1024x768@60Hz (current)
				1: 1024x768@61Hz

		What:		timing
		Type:		RW
		Description:	Index of the currently active timing. The
				display mode of the CRTC driving the panel is
				switched synchronously on write, and the
				fbdev emulation is updated so the new timing
				survives VT switches, lastclose and suspend/
				resume. The active timing also carries the
				connector's preferred mode flag, so
				fbcon and KMS clients pick it up.

				Writing an index >= count returns -ERANGE.
				Writing while no CRTC is driving the panel
				returns -ENODEV.
